.venv-cdfc/
.venv/
reports/*
# ...EXCEPT the two things a BUILD GATE reads. `ci/no-bare-absence.sh` resolves every
# `ledger:<row_id>` citation against the validation ledger, and the host-function registry
# refuses to load a function whose mutation score is not a produced file. A gate whose data is
# gitignored passes vacuously in a fresh clone — which is this project's own failure mode
# applied to its own CI. Found at P4 by asking what a clone would not have.
!reports/validation-ledger.jsonl
!reports/host_fns/
!reports/host_fns/*.json
# A campaign's reports ARE the evidence. `unobservable.jsonl` is what makes `U/G` auditable and
# what P10's residue feeds on, and `manifest.json` is what the published numbers are read from —
# so `docs/measurements/P6-fault-model-v3.md` can never quote a number no campaign produced.
# `_work/` is scratch and stays ignored: the mutants are re-derivable from the records and seeds.
!reports/campaigns/
!reports/campaigns/*/
!reports/campaigns/*/*.json
!reports/campaigns/*/*.jsonl
reports/campaigns/_work/
# The qualification artifact IS the predicate library, the rejected-candidate list and the
# attrition funnel. Three screens read it and `cdfc.qualify.artifact.load` RAISES when it is
# absent rather than serving an empty library — so leaving it ignored would make a fresh clone
# refuse three screens rather than pass them vacuously. Committed for the same reason the
# campaign reports are: it is evidence, and it is what the published numbers are read from.
!reports/qualification/
!reports/qualification/*.json
# The settled-fraction series, for the same reason: it is the evidence for criterion A8 — the
# number CAN go down — and a chart with no points is indistinguishable from a chart that has
# never fallen.
!reports/settled-history.jsonl
blobs/
*.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mutmut-cache
# fixtures/ is NEVER ignored — the nine real artifacts are the evidence base
!fixtures/
.DS_Store
.hypothesis/
